  "raw": " China. The earliest ancient city in China was in Nanjing with the oldest city in the world.\nBut for the past decades, the city has lost its glory amid the development process in China.\n\nNanjing is famous for the Ming and Qing dynasties during late Ming and Qing dynasties. Famous historical monuments include the Ming and Qing Imperial Family Temple, the Ming and Qing Memorial Hall and the Nanking Opera House.\nIt is said that during the early days, the Nanjing Golden River flowed out of the Yellow River, the largest river in the country flowing with the Yellow River.\nThe city is divided into two quarters--West and East. With ancient relics inside West Quarter, it is called the Imperial City, while East Quarter is also famous for its long riverfront and famous for its historical monuments as well as the \"Old Street\".\n\nNanjing, one of the nation's most important cities for over a thousand years, is recognized as one of",
